  "responseTimeMs": 25392,
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nA VAT-registered exporter that sells 100% of its goods abroad can obtain a refund or tax credit for input VAT. This is provided under the provisions of the NIRC.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor VAT-registered exporters, this provision is crucial as it enables them to recover input VAT, thereby reducing their overall tax burden. It incentivizes exports by ensuring that exporters are not disadvantaged by VAT costs on their inputs. To claim the refund or credit, exporters must ensure proper documentation and compliance with the BIR's requirements for VAT refunds, as outlined in the relevant regulations.",
